Article 2 (Persons Eligible for Creation, etc. of Family Relationship Registers) Persons eligible for creation or correction of family relationship registers (hereinafter referred to as "creation, etc. of family relationship registers") shall be any of the following persons who, as a result of damage caused by the Jeju April 3 Incident, have no family relationship register or whose entries in the family relationship register are contrary to the facts, and who have received a decision by the Committee for Investigation of the Truth of the Jeju April 3 Incident and Restoration of the Honor of Victims (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") concerning Article 5 (2) 7 of the Special Act on Discovering the Truth of the Jeju April 3 Incident and Restoring the Honor of Victims (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"):
1. A person determined to be a victim pursuant to Article 5 (2) of the Act;
2. A person determined to be a bereaved family member pursuant to Article 5 (2) of the Act;
3. Any other person designated as eligible for creation, etc. of a family relationship register by decision of the Committee.
